.TH HTTP_RECV 3
.SH NAME
http_recv \- read the decoded body of the response
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "ssize_t http_recv(http* " h ", char* " buf ", size_t " len ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION

.BR http_recv ()
stores up to len bytes of the body in buf. It decodes the chunked transfer encoding, a Content-Length or a body that ends with the connection, from what http_canread(3) received. It does not read from the socket. h->stream has to be set before the request is sent, otherwise http_canread(3) collects the body in the response.
.P
The response is complete when its status is HTTP_STATUS_FINISH.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The number of bytes, 0 if there is nothing for now, -1 on an error (a body that was cut off is one).
.SH SEE ALSO
http_canread(3), sse_feed(3)
